Subject: [candidate] checked reference callers and failure cleanup

Applies after candidates/0009. The retired 0010 is not required. Not selected by any engine recipe.
Status constructors preserve query/registration failures and register only
after fallible queries; ByName publishes only after checked acquisition while
the driver tree owns the object. Unsupported lookup inputs remain explicit.
Work submission failure releases exactly the reference it acquired and raises;
callback unwinding also releases that reference. PnP AddDevice unwinding
releases its named driver reference. Current-thread lookup closes
its temporary handle before raising and only caches successful results.

The private constructor callback now returns NTSTATUS (all four implementations
are updated). The constructor-call hunk must be retained when integrating K1's
handle-map locking changes. No new obref_cs-before-handle_map_cs acquisition.
Native behavior/parity remains pending. See tests/kernel/reference-callers/.

